reviewReports.claude-review-1.json:
{
  "subject_sha": "5737fc3ae01dc5b8b5b01124daeac1e805fc288f",
  "verdict": "changes-requested",
  "summary": "Round 1, read-only static review of the frontend delta 715a4b9e..5737fc3a (7 source files, 1 new test, 1 test update; e2e harness and evidence skimmed, not executed). It fixes #506: when Importa dimissione or Riprendi bozza is opened by route (initialPath), NewPatientFlow passes presentation 'page' and AccessibleDialogSurface renders PatientWorkspaceSurface instead of the modal. That surface portals into main.page-content, sizes itself to the main pane below .compact-topbar (ResizeObserver plus resize and scroll), and leaves the sidebar and topbar usable. Other children of main are made inert and restored on unmount, initial focus and return focus are kept, and Escape is ignored while a real aria-modal is open. The chooser path and all real confirmations keep modal semantics, and the loading and error states follow the same presentation. Sidebar and topbar clicks are captured and replayed only after beforeNavigate. The intake saves a pending (debounced) or failed draft first and stays open with its error if the save fails. The import keeps its existing close rules (busy or uploading blocks, unsaved review asks first). The mobile drawer (z-index 1200) stays above the workspace (z-index 30). No backend, schema or API change; no secrets. Two low findings are below; the core fix is sound. I ran no tests.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "frontend/src/components/shared/PatientWorkspaceSurface.tsx",
      "line": 75,
      "problem": "The guard treats every button or link in .teams-sidebar and .compact-topbar as navigation. That includes the ≤1023px hamburger that only opens the drawer, the search button and the avatar menu. On a tablet, during an upload (busy or pendingUpload) a hamburger tap is swallowed silently, with no message. In the import review step without a draft, opening the drawer immediately asks to close the import, and even after the close is confirmed the original click is not replayed.",
      "requested_change": "Apply beforeNavigate only to controls that actually change route (nav items, back, Esci), and let drawer, search and menu toggles pass through. When navigation is refused, tell the operator why (for example 'Caricamento in corso'). Consider replaying the original target after a confirmed close.",
      "test_expectation": "At 768px with an upload in progress, the hamburger opens the drawer and choosing a nav item is refused with a visible reason. In review without a draft, the hamburger opens the drawer without the close prompt, and a nav item shows the prompt; after the close is confirmed the operator lands on the chosen page."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "frontend/src/components/shared/intake/IntakeWorkspace.tsx",
      "line": 850,
      "problem": "'Navigation waits for the draft save' holds only for clicks in the sidebar or topbar. Browser Back or Forward (App.tsx popstate/hashchange restore) and programmatic navigate() calls unmount the workspace directly. The unmount cleanup (:202-207) then clears the 500ms debounce timer, so an edit typed within the last half second is dropped without saving. This is unchanged from before the PR, but the page presentation now invites leaving through the shell, and the PR description claims the guarantee in general.",
      "requested_change": "Flush the pending autosave on unmount (fire persistDraft with the latest dataRef, without awaiting UI state), or route popstate through the same beforeNavigate guard. Alternatively, narrow the PR/validation wording to sidebar and topbar navigation.",
      "test_expectation": "Type into an intake field and press browser Back within 500ms: reopening the draft shows the typed value, or the navigation is held until the save completes."
    }
  ]
}

reviewReports.claude-review-2.json:
{
  "subject_sha": "5105becde8bb222652ab2df7e72b0d32f05a7262",
  "verdict": "changes-requested",
  "summary": "Round 2, static review of 5105becd (no tests run by this reviewer). Both round-1 findings appear addressed. First, PatientWorkspaceSurface now intercepts only route controls (sidebar items except the AI item, sidebar and topbar links, topbar-back, logout), so drawer, search and menu toggles pass through. Second, after the import asks to confirm a close, the chosen navigation is replayed once the close is confirmed, and a blocked navigation during upload shows a notice. Third, IntakeWorkspace now flushes a pending debounced autosave on unmount with the captured queue and latest data, which covers browser Back and programmatic navigation. Separately, its beforeNavigate saves before leaving while a save is pending or has failed, and stays open if that save fails. Modal defaults, the chooser path and the confirmation dialog semantics are unchanged. One remaining correctness defect: the pending navigation promise in the import review is not settled when the confirm path 'save draft and close' fails or does not hand off to the workspace. This leaves the surface's navigating flag stuck and lets a stale navigation be replayed later. There is also a minor stale-notice issue. The supplied browser evidence uses synthetic localhost fixtures and does not exercise these paths.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "frontend/src/components/shared/DischargeImportModal.tsx",
      "line": 72,
      "problem": "When a route click is intercepted in the review step without a draft, beforeNavigate stores a resolver in pendingNavigation and returns a promise that only finishClose, cancelClose or unmount settle. The confirm action 'Salva bozza e chiudi' only clears closeRequested and calls reviewSave; the promise is resolved only if the save later reaches onWorkspace or close. If the save fails or stays on review (validation or server error), the promise never settles. PatientWorkspaceSurface (line 82) then keeps navigating=true, and every later sidebar or topbar route click is preventDefault'ed and silently dropped. In addition, a later user-initiated close via 'Chiudi senza salvare' resolves the stale resolver with true and replays the old navigation target, sending the user to a page chosen earlier instead of just closing.",
      "requested_change": "Settle the pending navigation whenever the confirmation flow ends without leaving. For example, have reviewSave return a promise/boolean and resolve pendingNavigation(false) on failure or when the review stays open. Also clear any stale resolver when a new non-navigation close request starts, so a later close never replays an old target. Optionally have the surface reset its navigating flag with a timeout or explicit cancel signal.",
      "test_expectation": "Browser regression in the review step: click a route control, choose 'Salva bozza e chiudi' with the draft save fixture returning an error. The review stays open with the error, a subsequent route-control click shows the close prompt again (not silently ignored), and closing via the header button then 'Chiudi senza salvare' closes without navigating to the earlier target."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "frontend/src/components/shared/DischargeImportModal.tsx",
      "line": 73,
      "problem": "navigationNotice is set when navigation is refused during busy or pending upload, but it is only cleared on the next navigation attempt. After the upload completes, the alert saying an upload is in progress stays visible and is misleading.",
      "requested_change": "Clear navigationNotice when busy and pendingUpload both become false (for example in an effect), or show it only while the blocking condition holds.",
      "test_expectation": "With an upload in progress, a route click shows the notice; once the upload completes, the notice disappears without any further interaction."
    }
  ]
}

reviewReports.claude-review-3.json:
{
  "subject_sha": "ff91e103827612337346520f2939694c6ae6bb92",
  "verdict": "changes-requested",
  "summary": "Round 3 is a static review of ff91e103. I ran no tests. Both round-2 findings look fixed. When 'Salva bozza e chiudi' is chosen after a route click, the new closeSavePending effect cancels the stored navigation once the review stops being busy. A failed save therefore keeps the review open, releases the surface's navigating flag and lets a later route click ask again. A successful handoff through onWorkspace finishes the close and replays the route exactly once. A close from the header or footer now cancels any older pending navigation first, so an old destination is not replayed. The upload notice clears once busy and pendingUpload are both false. The confirmation is the same ConfirmDialog, now portalled to the document body. It keeps its modal Escape and focus handling, and the workspace's Escape handler still skips when a modal is open. The IntakeWorkspace changes (unmount flush, clearing the debounce timer, saveAndClose returning a boolean) and the presentation plumbing are unchanged from round 2 and look correct. The e2e harness adds controlled cases for a failed save, a successful save, upload completion and the confirmation fitting at 390px, using synthetic localhost fixtures. Its exemptions for the negative case are tightly limited. The supplied validation report and proof comment say the build, frontend tests, browser regression and six CI checks passed. I did not run any of them. Two low findings remain. Both are about refused navigation not explaining itself, which round 1 asked for and only the import surface partly does.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "frontend/src/components/shared/intake/IntakeWorkspace.tsx",
      "line": 848,
      "problem": "In page presentation, IntakeWorkspace's beforeNavigate returns false while a submission is running: patient creation, a proposal decision or an in-flight saveAndClose. saveAndClose also returns false straight away when that same submitting flag is set. PatientWorkspaceSurface has already cancelled the click and stopped it propagating, so the sidebar or topbar route click is dropped with no visible reason. Round 1 asked that a refused navigation tell the operator why. The import surface now shows a notice, but the intake surface does not.",
      "requested_change": "When the intake refuses navigation because a submission or save is in progress, show an announced notice in the workspace, as DischargeImportModal does with navigationNotice. Clear it once the submission ends. Alternatively, wait for the in-flight operation to finish and then decide, instead of refusing silently.",
      "test_expectation": "Hold a confirm or proposal-decision request in the fixture and click a sidebar route control. The workspace stays open and shows a visible alert explaining that navigation waits for the operation. The alert disappears when the request completes, and a later route click navigates."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "frontend/src/components/shared/DischargeImportModal.tsx",
      "line": 397,
      "problem": "beforeNavigate refuses navigation whenever busy or pendingUpload is true. In both cases it shows the fixed message 'Caricamento in corso. Attendi il completamento prima di cambiare pagina.' busy is also true for non-upload operations such as reopen, process or retry, discard, and the review draft save. In those cases the alert wrongly tells the operator that an upload is in progress.",
